## 18. The middle tiers {#tiers}

Most of the institution's work is done below the founder and the board, by people who see decisions without making them. Small-group leaders, worship leaders, staff, elders and deacons, and Christian school teachers each carry part of the load, and each stands at one point where the next decision could be declined. The table sets out what each tier does, what it sees, what it is asked to do and where it could refuse.

